  now(), now(), 4, false, 'Zidane''s France squad: injuries, returns and possible surprises before the announcement', 'Zinédine Zidane names his second France squad on Friday 6 November at 6pm, for Italy v France and France v Turkey. Dembélé and Olise are doubtful, Tchouaméni and Zaïre-Emery are expected back, and Thauvin is pushing for a call. Passe D sums it up.', '<p><em>Published before the official announcement. The names below are leads reported by the French press, not the squad. Passe D will update this article from 6pm (Paris time).</em></p><p>It is the big moment of the day. On <strong>Friday 6 November at 6pm</strong>, at the French federation''s headquarters, <strong>Zinédine Zidane</strong> names his second squad as France coach. It covers the last two group matches of the Nations League. He can call up to 26 players, who report to Clairefontaine on Monday.</p><h2>The fixtures</h2><ul><li><strong>Thursday 12 November, 8.45pm</strong>: Italy v France, in Milan</li><li><strong>Sunday 15 November, 8.45pm</strong>: France v Turkey, in Bordeaux</li></ul><h2>Where France stand</h2><p>The Zidane era has started well. In four matches, France beat Turkey (1-0) and Belgium (1-0, then 4-1) and drew with Italy (1-1). With 10 points, they top the group ahead of Italy (7) and Belgium (6). The trip to Milan could decide first place.</p><p>For his first squad in September, Zidane picked 23 players, including five newcomers: Guillaume Restes (Toulouse), Jérémy Jacquet (Liverpool), Andy Diouf (Inter), Lucas Da Cunha (Como) and Estéban Lepaul (Rennes).</p><h2>A crowded treatment room</h2><p>This is Zidane''s headache. According to the French press, several key players are affected:</p><ul><li><strong>Ousmane Dembélé</strong> (thigh): very doubtful, possibly out</li><li><strong>Michael Olise</strong>: injured against Dortmund on 31 October, doubtful</li><li><strong>Jules Koundé</strong> (ankle): doubtful</li><li><strong>William Saliba</strong>, <strong>Manu Koné</strong> (hamstring) and <strong>Estéban Lepaul</strong> (ankle): likely out</li><li><strong>Maxence Lacroix</strong>: out</li></ul><p>Without Dembélé and Olise, the attack would lose two of its best weapons. Mbappé, Doué and Barcola would carry the load.</p><h2>Expected returns</h2><p><strong>Aurélien Tchouaméni</strong> should be back. In September, Zidane left him out for lack of match rhythm. <strong>Warren Zaïre-Emery</strong>, who withdrew last time, would also be called according to TF1. In goal, Lens keeper <strong>Robin Risser</strong>, a late withdrawal last time, is expected.</p><h2>Possible surprises</h2><p>These are the names doing the rounds. Nothing is official.</p><ul><li><strong>Florian Thauvin (Lens)</strong>: at 33, he is having a superb start to the season (4 goals and 8 assists according to MadeInLensois, top of the Ligue 1 assist chart). He has said publicly he dreams of a return. It would be the big surprise.</li><li><strong>Marcus Thuram (Inter)</strong>: a natural candidate to make up for Dembélé''s likely absence.</li><li><strong>Lucas Hernandez (PSG)</strong>: versatile, he can cover in the middle or on the left, useful with so many defensive injuries.</li><li><strong>Wesley Fofana (Chelsea)</strong>: not called since June 2023, his name is back in the frame with the centre-back absences.</li><li><strong>Leny Yoro</strong>: impressive against Belgium, he could benefit from Saliba''s absence.</li><li><strong>Maghnes Akliouche (PSG)</strong>: competing with Zaïre-Emery for a midfield spot.</li><li><strong>Eli Junior Kroupi</strong>: back from injury, one more attacking option.</li><li><strong>Pierre Kalulu</strong>: an option at right back if Koundé is not fit.</li></ul><h2>The expected core</h2><p>Around these doubts, the backbone should stay the same: Mbappé, Doué and Barcola up front; Cherki, Camavinga and Da Cunha in midfield; Upamecano, Konaté and Jacquet at centre-back; Truffert on the left.</p><h2>Our view</h2><p>With so many absentees, Zidane will have to open the door. Tchouaméni''s return looks logical, and the Thauvin question is the most interesting one: reward current form, or stick with youth? We will know at 6pm. Passe D will bring you the full squad. ⚽🇫🇷</p><h2>Sources</h2><p><a href="https://www.fff.fr/article/17631-la-liste-de-zinedine-zidane-le-6-novembre.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FFF</a>, <a href="https://www.ouest-france.fr/sport/football/equipe-de-france/date-matches-joueurs-tout-savoir-sur-la-deuxieme-liste-de-zinedine-zidane-a-la-tete-de-lequipe-de-france-d3f36c54-d612-11f1-84f3-5611f158a658" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ouest-France</a>, <a href="https://www.tf1info.fr/sport/equipe-de-france-la-date-de-la-prochaine-liste-des-bleus-de-zinedine-zidane-pour-les-matchs-contre-l-italie-et-la-turquie-devoilee-2471459.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TF1info</a>, <a href="https://rmcsport.bfmtv.com/football/equipe-de-france/equipe-de-france-la-prochaine-liste-de-zidane-devoilee-le-6-novembre_AV-202610220657.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RMC Sport</a>, <a href="https://www.topmercato.com/2153170-equipe-de-france-une-place-pour-lucas-hernandez-et-tchouameni-fais-ta-liste-de-zidane/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TopMercato</a> and <a href="https://madeinlensois.ouest-france.fr/infos/article-equipe-de-france-florian-thauvin-pourrait-etre-l-une-des-surprises-de-la-prochaine-liste-de-zidane-544245.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MadeInLensois</a>.</p><p>— Passe D</p>', true
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;
